      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes perfect sense to feel that way when you look at the cold, hard math of a universe that will outlast everything we ever build. The struggle against such inevitable nothingness is a profound and lonely realization, but it's also the very thing that gives your pain its weight and your life its texture. You don't need to convince yourself it matters for the sake of the universe; it matters because you are here, feeling the ache of it all, and that sensation is real even if the end result isn't.",
      "source": "target",
